  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{Fe}^{3+}\\left(d^{5}\\right)$ has 5 unpaired electrons therefore magneticmoment $=\\sqrt{n(n+2)}=\\sqrt{5(5+2)}=5.91$ which is maximum among given options. As $\\mathrm{Sc}^{3+}, \\mathrm{Ti}^{3+}, \\mathrm{Cr}^{3+}$ and $\\mathrm{V}^{3+}$ contain $0,1,3$, and 2 number of unpaired electrons respectively.",
